{"id":115,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"There are records of a lost human child being raised by a childless Kangaskhan."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Although it’s carrying its baby in a pouch on its belly, Kangaskhan is swift on its feet. It intimidates its opponents with quick jabs."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Raises its young in its belly pouch. Won’t run from any fight to keep its young protected."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"You shouldn’t get close to the child when it’s playing outside its mother’s pouch. Its mother is always nearby watching over it."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Kangaskhan protects its child by keeping it in its pouch. It has zero forgiveness for those who harm its child and will beat them down."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"The child in its pouch leaves home after roughly three years. That is the only time the mother is heard to cry wildly."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Kangaskhan’s maternal love is so deep that it will brave death to protect its offspring."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"If you come across a young Kangaskhan playing by itself, you must never disturb it or attempt to catch it. The baby Pokémon’s parent is sure to be in the area, and it will become violently enraged at you."},{"games":["Y","HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"If it is safe, the young gets out of the belly pouch to play. The adult keeps a close eye on the youngster."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It raises its offspring in its belly pouch. It lets the baby out to play only when it feels safe."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"To protect its young, it will never give up during battle, no matter how badly wounded it is."},{"games":["LeafGreen"],"text":"The infant rarely ventures out of its mother’s protective pouch until it is three years old."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"The female raises its offspring in a pouch on its belly. It is skilled at attacking using COMET PUNCH."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"If you come across a young KANGASKHAN playing by itself, never try to catch it. The baby’s parent is sure to be in the area, and it will become violently enraged."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"To avoid crushing the baby it carries in its pouch, it always sleeps standing up."},{"games":["Blue","Red"],"text":"The infant rarely ventures out of its mother's protective pouch until it is 3 years old."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Early Bird","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon awakens from sleep twice as fast as other Pokémon."},{"name":"Scrappy","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon can hit Ghost-type Pokémon with Normal- and Fighting-type moves. It is also unaffected by Intimidate."},{"name":"Inner Focus","hidden":true,"description":"The Pokémon's intense focus prevents it from flinching or being affected by Intimidate."}],"eggGroups":["Monster"],"genderRate":8,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"grassland","color":"Brown","shape":"Upright","evolution":{"id":115,"name":"Kangaskhan","condition":null,"children":[]},"moves":{"game":"Sword / Shield","level":[[1,1],[1,39],[4,45],[8,252],[12,44],[16,23],[20,116],[24,29],[28,389],[32,458],[36,242],[40,203],[44,179],[48,200],[52,387]],"machine":[372,213,419,251,59,34,280,523,242,91,409,89,203,263,126,7,53,374,411,116,416,258,270,56,63,58,8,196,231,67,25,5,200,182,240,156,514,179,157,317,496,219,201,247,421,214,173,76,164,241,57,168,87,9,85,253,250,526],"egg":[509,68,50,38,283,359],"tutor":[805]},"cards":[{"id":"me1-182","name":"Mega Kangaskhan ex","set":"Mega Evolution","date":"2025-09-26","rarity":"Special Illustration Rare","number":"182","artist":null,"img":"me1/182"},{"id":"me55-114","name":"Kangaskhan","set":"30th Celebration","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Common","number":"114","artist":"Pani Kobayashi","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-114/small","large":"https://images.scrydex